  "narrative": "This wave adds marker-F negative controls, batch interaction tests, an adherent-culture MSI-high/WRN analysis, and two specificity analyses. The marker-F controls are close to null for all three major outcomes: WRN (R27), SMARCA2 (R31), and NFE2L2 (R35). The marker-F interactions with the accepted associations are also near null for SMARCA2 (R32), WRN (R28), and NFE2L2 (R36). Together with the earlier marker-D null controls and null interactions, these results reduce concern that the very large SMARCA4-loss/SMARCA2, MSI-high/WRN, and KEAP1-loss/NFE2L2 associations are artifacts of arbitrary constructed-marker structure or marker-correlated population structure. Batch tests for MSI-high/WRN and KEAP1/NFE2L2 are near null (R29, R37), although the WRN batch interaction is imprecise because the exposed cells in batch_a are small. The SMARCA2 batch_a interaction is statistically nonzero but small in magnitude and opposite to the registered negative-direction claim; it does not support the claim as registered and is far smaller than the main SMARCA4 effect, so I reject it for that claim rather than treating it as a meaningful confounder. The adherent-culture MSI-high/WRN effect is very large and precise (R30: signed estimate +0.813, 95% CI [0.780,0.846] under direction -1), consistent with the overall MSI-high/WRN effect (R8) and the adenocarcinoma-restricted effect (R22). The ARID1A-loss effect among SMARCA4-intact cells is null (R34), supporting specificity of the SMARCA2 signal to SMARCA4 loss rather than generalized SWI/SNF loss. The BRCA2-loss effect among MSI-negative cells is null (R38), suggesting the WRN association is not a broad DNA-repair-loss marker but is more specific to MSI-high status in this dataset. Given this robustness pattern, I request independent validation for H9, MSI-high versus WRN dependency, because it is the next accepted large association and has now survived marker controls, subtype, culture, and specificity checks.",
  "research_notes": "Updated evidence status. Validated primary dataset associations: H7 SMARCA4 loss -> much stronger SMARCA2 dependency; H19 reversed KEAP1 loss -> weaker NFE2L2 dependency. H9 MSI-high -> much stronger WRN dependency remains accepted on discovery and has now received additional internal robustness support from adenocarcinoma subgroup (R22) and adherent culture (R30); validation requested this iteration. Constructed negative controls: marker D and marker F main effects are near null for SMARCA2, WRN, and NFE2L2; marker D and marker F interactions with accepted effects are near null, reducing marker-structure concern. Batch tests: WRN/MSI and KEAP1/NFE2L2 batch_a interactions near null; SMARCA2 batch_a interaction is small, opposite the registered claim direction, and not interpreted as meaningful. Specificity: ARID1A loss among SMARCA4-intact cells is null for SMARCA2, and BRCA2 loss among MSI-negative cells is null for WRN. Accepted conditional/context claims: H20 and H26 KEAP1/NFE2L2 large in TP53-intact and TP53-loss; H21 and H22 SMARCA4/SMARCA2 large in adenocarcinoma and ARID1A-intact; H23 and H55 MSI-high/WRN large in adenocarcinoma and adherent cells. Next after H9 validation: analyze marker E main controls and interactions if useful, media-serum interactions, possibly CRISPR library or culture context for remaining accepted associations, then EGFR subtype/KRAS-WT and lower-priority driver/MYC hypotheses. Keep all conclusions dataset-specific associations; do not claim causality or generalizability."
